<https://github.com/john1hsu/business-knowledge-graph/id/organizational-ambidexterity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An organization's capacity to exploit its existing businesses efficiently while simultaneously exploring new technologies and markets, achieved either by separating exploratory and exploitative units under a shared senior team (structural ambidexterity) or by a context that lets individuals split their time between alignment and adaptation (contextual ambidexterity)." .
